# Put the KSU autoinstall script where KernelSU will run it.
#
# init deliberately does NOT exec anything here. A service like
#   service ksu_autoinstall /system/bin/sh /system_ext/bin/ksu-autoinstall.sh
# fails with "File /system/bin/sh (labeled u:object_r:shell_exec:s0) has
# incorrect label or no domain transition from u:r:init:s0", because init may
# not exec a shell without a domain of its own. `copy` is a built-in init
# command, so it needs no exec and no new sepolicy.
#
# KernelSU runs everything in /data/adb/service.d at its `services` stage, in
# its own context (u:r:ksu:s0) -- the same context ksud itself runs in, which is
# exactly what `ksud module install` needs. That stage comes after post-fs-data,
# so the script runs on this same boot.
#
# system_ext, not vendor: a vendor rc runs as vendor_init and cannot touch
# /data/adb.
#
# The copy happens on every boot so an updated ROM refreshes the script; the
# script itself is idempotent through its markers.

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/adb 0700 root root
    mkdir /data/adb/service.d 0700 root root
    copy /system_ext/bin/ksu-autoinstall.sh /data/adb/service.d/ksu-autoinstall.sh
    chmod 0700 /data/adb/service.d/ksu-autoinstall.sh
    chown root root /data/adb/service.d/ksu-autoinstall.sh
